※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4615 LANG_ARENA_VALUE_GIVEN_BACK

※ An arm that leaves the function reaches no join, so what it did to a name is not what holds
※ after the `if`: there `x` still holds what it was given first, made in `s0`.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let s0: mut arena = ⎕arena
    let s1: mut arena = ⎕arena
    defer ⎕empty(s1)
    let c: bool = false
    let x: mut str = "a" ⧺ "b" in s0
    if c:
        x ← "c" ⧺ "d" in s1
        ⎕empty(s0)
        return 2u6
    ⎕empty(s0)
    if x = "ab": 0u6 else: 1u6
